                <UserObject event_date="1813-12-16" event_end_date="1813-12-16" date_label="16 December 1813" location="Ship rations: 16-29 Dec (14 days)" name_as_recorded="Demel, Lewen" evidence_type="Named pay-list entry" source_shape_ids="[&quot;volume10&quot;]" source_files="[&quot;primary_sources/WO_12-7088/P1070654.JPG&quot;, &quot;primary_sources/WO_12-7088/P1070653.JPG&quot;, &quot;primary_sources/WO_12-7088/P1070699.JPG&quot;, &quot;primary_sources/WO_12-7088/P1070700.JPG&quot;]" link="primary_sources/WO_12-7088/P1070654.JPG" citation="WO 12/7088, entry 193; column headings in P1070653. Company 9; voucher 1; pay for 99 days from 16 December 1813 to 24 March 1814, ?4 7s 6d. The bracketed As No 5 refers to entry 5 on P1070699 and its ship-ration annotations, enlarged in P1070700: 14 days to 29 December and 9 days from 16 March. These are ration periods, not independently established sailing dates. Original user wording remains in example_original_text." example_original_text="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;December 16, 1813&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;Fort Cumberland, Eastney, Portsmouth&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Demel, Lewen&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;private, 7th Battalion, 60th Regiment of Foot, Company 9&lt;br&gt;Enlisted by Capt. Marschalck out of the POW depot at Portsmouth" label="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px;line-height:19px&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:22px;line-height:25px&quot;&gt;16 December 1813&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ship rations: 16-29 Dec (14 days)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:22px;line-height:25px&quot;&gt;Demel, Lewen&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Private, Company 9, 7th Battalion, 60th Foot. &amp;quot;Vol. from Pris. of War.&amp;quot; Pay: 16 Dec 1813-24 Mar 1814, 99 days, ?4 7s 6d. Entry 193 refers to voucher 1 and the ship-ration note &amp;quot;As No 5.&amp;quot;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;primary_sources/WO_12-7088/P1070654.JPG&quot;&gt;WO 12/7088&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" tooltip="WO 12/7088, entry 193; column headings in P1070653. Company 9; voucher 1; pay for 99 days from 16 December 1813 to 24 March 1814, ?4 7s 6d. The bracketed As No 5 refers to entry 5 on P1070699 and its ship-ration annotations, enlarged in P1070700: 14 days to 29 December and 9 days from 16 March. These are ration periods, not independently established sailing dates. Original user wording remains in example_original_text.&#xa;&#xa;Supporting files:&#xa;primary_sources/WO_12-7088/P1070654.JPG&#xa;primary_sources/WO_12-7088/P1070653.JPG&#xa;primary_sources/WO_12-7088/P1070699.JPG&#xa;primary_sources/WO_12-7088/P1070700.JPG" id="eknEnN58jiTXOptYuaQ4-1">
